> Output counts, guards and storage

Each iteration increments y exactly once, so there are at most r+1 iterations
for nonnegative radius and exactly eight raw emissions per iteration. Ordinary
production takes O(r+1) time and O(1) state plus O(r+1) returned pixels. The
study’s sorting/deduplication costs O(r log(r+1)) work and additional output; do
not attribute that sorting cost to the rasterizer itself.

Decisions use signed64-bit arithmetic. Before any coordinate addition or
capture, nonnegative radius requires all four bounding coordinates cx±r,cy±r to
fit int; overflow throws. Negative radius preserves the original empty
convention. Radius zero preserves eight coincident centre emissions rather than
pretending there are eight distinct pixels. Its single step includes the actual
final update even though no later pixel is emitted.

Optional capture admits three input scalars, then each actual complete
iteration’s eight point records and one step record before emission. Its count
is3+9 times the number of actual iterations. Default quota is one million; zero
disables only that optional cap. Fields, capacities, runtime state and bytes are
excluded. Exceeding admission throws without returning a partial trace. Neither
a quota nor widened arithmetic guarantees a practical runtime for an enormous
representable radius.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/midpoint_circle_counts.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, raw, distinct;
    std::print("| prescribed radius | actual iterations | actual raw emissions | distinct pixels | " "duplicate emissions | actual capture entries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (int r : {0, 1, 2, 3, 6, 12}) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::midpoint_circle_trace(0, 0, r);
        auto s = dm::algorithms::midpoint_circle_study(0, 0, r);
        x.push_back(r);
        raw.push_back(t.analysis.points.size());
        distinct.push_back(s.unique_points.size());
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r,
                   t.analysis.iterations, t.analysis.points.size(),
                   s.unique_points.size(), s.duplicate_emissions,
                   t.captured_entries);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, raw, "raw emissions");
    p.line(x, distinct, "distinct pixels", {22, 163, 74});
    p.x_label("prescribed radius").y_label("actual point count").title(
        "Reflection emissions and distinct pixels differ").save_svg(
        "build/midpoint_circle_counts.svg");
}
```
